From b6283f5b0452c240845c37e00fd5d86f8eaba5a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:00:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Security hardening and bug fixes

Security
- Remove Telegram bot token from the client bundle (was VITE_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN);
  send-reminder now reads TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN from Edge Function secrets, verifies the
  caller via initData, requires course ownership + enrollment, rate-limits per student.
- Add auth-telegram Edge Function: verifies initData HMAC and issues a Supabase JWT.
- Replace open USING (true) RLS policies with auth.uid()-scoped ones (migration 004);
  anon has no table access, telegram_id is no longer readable by clients.
- telegram-webhook: require X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token, private chats only.
- Validate URLs before opening links (block javascript:/data: schemes).

Bug fixes
- CourseEditor: action errors no longer replace the whole editor and discard input;
  ownership check, slug/URL validation, duplicate-slug message, reorder error handling.
- 'Continue learning' now resumes an unfinished lesson instead of skipping it.
- Lesson 'in progress' state now shown; draft courses are no longer reachable by deep link.
- Enrollment/progress writes are race-safe (conflict handling / upsert).
- LessonPage: failed 'mark complete' keeps the lesson on screen.
- Webhook: t.me links and native attachments (video/pdf/photo) are detected;
  re-forwarding no longer resets imported messages to pending.
- Deep links read start_param from the SDK first.
- Parallelised N+1 queries on dashboard/home; removed dead code; lint is clean.

Docs: .env.example, README with deploy steps.
